messages:
Maria: new spike from support: multiple CF Workers users hit runtime failures with our JS SDK. Symptoms range from "require is not defined" to TypeScript errors referencing Node types.
Kevin: typical. Workers are ESM + no Node builtins. Do we currently ship an ESM entrypoint and an edge-targeted build?
Sam: not yet. We only publish CJS and a browser bundle that still pulls a few Node polyfills. Plan: add conditional exports and a dedicated worker bundle that excludes node-only deps.
Olivia: major constraints to document: no process, no fs, no Buffer; global fetch exists but behavior differs (signals/streaming). Also TypeScript consumers get conflicts when our d.ts references NodeJS.ReadableStream.
Maria: here's a short repro a user sent (they bundled with CJS):
```js
// user index (problematic)
const { RedwoodClient } = require('redwood');
addEventListener('fetch', e => e.respondWith(handle(e.request)));
async function handle(req) {
  const c = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: __ENV.REDWOOD_KEY });
  const r = await c.generate('hello');
  return new Response(r.text);
}
```
Error: "require is not defined" on deploy.
Kevin: immediate fixes: 1) publish dist/redwood.esm.mjs and make it the import entry; 2) add exports map so bundlers resolve a worker/browser-specific bundle; 3) produce dist/redwood.worker.mjs that is tree-shaken for edge. Suggested exports (conceptual):
```json
"exports": {
  "import": "./dist/redwood.esm.mjs",
  "require": "./dist/redwood.cjs.js",
  "worker": "./dist/redwood.worker.mjs",
  "browser": {
    "import": "./dist/redwood.browser.mjs"
  }
}
```
Sam: worker build notes: avoid any transitive dep that pulls in stream/fs polyfills. Replace Buffer usage with Uint8Array and remove Node ReadableStream from public types. Also, make the HTTP retry layer prefer globalThis.fetch and accept a user-supplied fetch to handle platform differences.
Olivia: types: create a small types/worker.d.ts that provides minimal ambient types (e.g., ReadableStreamLike) and don't import Node types in the edge conditional. We can add a types export for the worker branch so TS consumers targeting workers don't get Node type errors.
Maria: runtime detection helper we can add to SDK: 
```ts
export const isEdgeRuntime = typeof globalThis?.fetch === 'function' && typeof process === 'undefined';
```
Usage: `const fetchImpl = opts.fetch ?? (isEdgeRuntime ? globalThis.fetch : nodeFetch);`
Kevin: also change our retry/backoff wrapper so it works with the platform fetch: don't rely on Node-only AbortSignal internals. Use the standard AbortController where available. Provide tests for both node-fetch and global fetch semantics.
Sam: testing: add a lightweight CI job using miniflare to run smoke tests against our worker bundle (ci:worker-smoke). That will catch accidental Node-only code being pulled into worker builds. We can run 2 tests: a simple generate() and a streaming tokens smoke.
Olivia: sample quickstart for README (Worker + ESM):
```js
import { RedwoodClient } from 'redwood';
export default {
  async fetch(request, env) {
    const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: env.REDWOOD_KEY, fetch: globalThis.fetch });
    const resp = await client.generate('hello from worker');
    return new Response(resp.text);
  }
};
```
Also include esbuild config suggestion: `{ format: 'esm', target: 'es2020', platform: 'browser' }`.
Maria: docs should explicitly list do/don't: do pass fetch/env into constructor; do use ESM import; don't import form-data/node-fetch at top-level; don't assume Buffer exists; avoid dynamic require().
Kevin: implementation owner volunteers? Sam will add the build + example under examples/worker/ and CI job. Olivia will prepare types/worker.d.ts and update d.ts references. I'll prepare the exports/packaging PR to add worker branch. Maria will draft the support KB and README additions.
support-bot: opened issue #4527 in repo with label 'edge-sdk' and linked this thread.
Maria: great. Once the packaging PR lands we'll ask support to escalate remaining tickets and provide a short code fix users can apply (switch require -> import, pass fetch). Thanks team.
